From d85ab02be8a7ed550804dd589d3612fbcfc18c25 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: <worker git identity, redacted>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 22:14:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH 3/3] Leave worktrees whose ownership is unproven for the
 operator

Review found two gaps. Records made before this branch (no owner token,
or no `.git` change time) were still compared on inode numbers alone,
so a checkout rebuilt and repaired at the same path could be removed.
And `git worktree repair --relative-paths` rewrites the `.git` file of
the run's own worktree, which cleanup then called replaced: it marked
the worktree gone while it survived, and its branch removal failed.

A worktree is now 'unproven' when its admin directory and token still
match but the `.git` file was rewritten, or when the record has no
token or change time. Cleanup offers no command for it; recording the
cleanup marks it, and the branch checked out there, 'unproven' instead
of gone. The report lists them under "Unproven resources" with the
reason and no command to copy.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
